<section class="leak-faq" aria-labelledby="leak-faq-title">
  <div class="faq-inner">
    <p class="faq-eyebrow">Have questions?</p>
    <h2 id="leak-faq-title">Leak Detection Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <p class="faq-intro">Everything you need to know about leak detection at Delta Plumbing.</p>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <article class="faq-item" data-open="true">
        <h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" id="faq-question-1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-1">How do I know if I have a hidden water leak in my home?<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-1"><div class="faq-answer-inner"><p>You usually do not see the water itself. You see the side effects: a jump in your water bill you can't explain, a damp or warm spot on the floor, a musty smell that won't go away, mold or mildew where it shouldn't be, the faint sound of running water with every fixture off, low pressure at one or two faucets, or a green patch in the yard that stays green through a dry week. Any one of these is worth a phone call. Two or more usually means you have a hidden leak that needs attention before it gets expensive.</p></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="faq-item" data-open="false">
        <h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" id="faq-question-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-2">What does leak detection cost at Delta Plumbing?<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-2"><div class="faq-answer-inner"><p>Standard residential leak detection is $199. Mention code <strong>LEAKDETECT39</strong> when you book. The visit includes the technician's time, acoustic and thermal imaging equipment, and a written report. Repairs are not included. If you choose to move forward with a repair, we'll give you a separate written estimate before work starts, with no pressure to commit on the spot.</p></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="faq-item" data-open="false">
        <h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" id="faq-question-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-3">Will you have to tear up my floors or walls to find the leak?<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-3"><div class="faq-answer-inner"><p>No. We use sound, heat, and pressure to narrow down the leak before opening anything. Once we know where it is, we open only a small section at that confirmed spot. Many leaks can be located without unnecessary damage to your floors, walls, or yard.</p></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="faq-item" data-open="false">
        <h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" id="faq-question-4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-4">What kind of equipment do you use to find leaks?<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-4"><div class="faq-answer-inner"><p>We use professional acoustic listening equipment, including the Aquaphon A200, to hear water escaping a pressurized pipe—even through concrete. We pair that with thermal imaging cameras, ground microphones for buried supply lines, and tracer gas when acoustic detection alone is not enough.</p></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="faq-item" data-open="false">
        <h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" id="faq-question-5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-5">How long does a leak detection visit usually take?<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-5"><div class="faq-answer-inner"><p>Most residential appointments take 60 to 90 minutes from arrival to written report. A simple in-wall leak may be confirmed in under an hour. Buried supply lines and larger commercial pipe networks can take longer; we'll give you a realistic estimate when we book.</p></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="faq-item" data-open="false">
        <h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" id="faq-question-6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-6">Can you find leaks under driveways, patios, or in the yard?<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-6"><div class="faq-answer-inner"><p>Yes. Our technicians use ground microphones and acoustic locating equipment to listen for escaping water through asphalt, concrete, and soil, including on the buried supply line between your meter and home. After pinpointing the leak, we can usually keep digging to a minimum; trenchless repair may be an option in some cases.</p></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="faq-item" data-open="false">
        <h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" id="faq-question-7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-7">Can you locate a gas leak, too?<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-7" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-7"><div class="faq-answer-inner"><p>Yes. If you smell gas, leave the home first and call your gas utility from outside. After the home is cleared as safe, our licensed technicians can locate gas line leaks with combustible gas detectors and tracer gas. Gas line work is a separate service from water leak detection.</p></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="faq-item" data-open="false">
        <h3><button class="faq-question" type="button" id="faq-question-8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-8">Do you handle commercial leak detection?<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-8" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-8"><div class="faq-answer-inner"><p>Yes. Delta provides leak detection for Atlanta homes and businesses. Larger commercial systems with more extensive pipe networks can take longer to inspect, and we'll provide a time estimate when scheduling.</p></div></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.leak-faq .faq-item').forEach((item) => {
    const button = item.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.faq-question');
    if (!button) return;
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const expanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
      item.dataset.open = String(!expanded);
    });
  });
</script>

